 ((:id "goal" :type :work-set :children ("future"))
  (:id "future" :type :roadmap :title "Future work"
   :rows (
     ("admission-refuses-functional-done-when" "add refuses a DONE-WHEN that runs functional tests, which cannot run inside the wall")
     ("deal-skips-old-binary-rows" "The dealer never deals to a row whose advertised binary is older than the run's version")
     ("missing-toolchain-refuses" "A missing toolchain inside the wall is a refusal at admission or a fault, never a bounce")
     ("per-row-stream-exclusion" "Exclude a stream from a row (needs a schema change)")
     ("runner-registrations-as-records" "Runner registrations stored as nova-config records")
     ("steps-model-covers-holds-and-limits" "Steps.tla gains the holds/limits/silence/Gone step (the model gap under #702's bug)")
     ("policy-limits-read-by-steps" "The nine validated policy limits read by the steps instead of Engine.* constants")
     ("policy-diff" "policy diff vA vB: a line diff of two policy versions (deleted 2026-11-08; policy show each and diff them)")
     ("provider-balance-reconcile" "cost reconcile: provider balance falls set beside the priced API records, a cost-gap judgement hourly (deleted 2026-11-08 with modules/cost; the sprint.balances table stays)")
     ("land-rate-and-flap-alarms" "Delete the land-rate and flap alarms, the flaps column and SetRowFlaps (decision 6, not done: engine code under PR #714)")
     ("engine-dead-code-pass" "Engine dead code (dropped from the 2026-11-08 pass): card/values.go mirror of store/check.go; replay.go write-applier; WaiveRed and the red column; the Edit event; Rescore and score; Released, single AskRead, SetCardAfter, ImportedReason; the deadcode list (verbs, edge, policy, card, steps, store, worker, dash, run); schema column drops")
     ("faults-limit-hold-witness" "The faults limit, its hold and the Steps limits witness (wip: model the limits step)")
     ("up-simplification" "up simplified: no two-phase handoff, no provider key step, no saved choices or --run-on, no --version adoption, no setup-time backup verify (S6 S3 S10 S14 S21)")
     ("stop-holds-landing-in-flight" "A stop holds a landing or promotion already in flight: it merges nothing until start (PR #741, parked)")
     ("add-adopts-card-branch" "add adopts a card's existing branch as its head, so a continuing card starts from it (PR #726, parked)")
     ("steps-model-covers-rest" "Steps.tla gains the rest after faults: a resting row is offered to policy but not dealt to (the model gap under #740)")
     ("next-json-answers-small" "next --json answers small: the finished cards of the epoch listed in brief, or only the last few (82-214 KB on nine benches on 2026-11-09, past the worker's old 64 KiB cap; the worker now reads 16 MiB and names a truncated answer, so the fix here is the size, not the parse)")
     ("ci-flakes" "Functional flakes fixed: TestFunctionalClearWhileWorkersBeat (clear's seq fence refused: store at seq N+1, expected N, a beat landing between read and clear), TestFunctionalEvaluatorMemoryCap (failed once on main), a postgres start failure in a functional run; and the trace job near the 2-minute runner limit (55-130 s, cancelled on 7 of the 2026-11-09 landing runs)")
     ("coordinator-seat-model" "A model of the coordinator's seat: one coordinator; hook, unhook and up --take-over, the take-over moving the seat whether the old coordinator is on the bus or gone, with a reversed witness (two coordinators at once); no module covers it (Setup.tla has the walk's steps, Store.tla the PutRow write)")
     ("auto-down-after-missed-takes" "A row that misses N takes in a row is unhooked by the sprint (its hand returned) with a DOWN line to the coordinator; a take or a re-hook resets the count (new mechanism: needs the owner's agreement)")
     ("no-progress-line" "NO-PROGRESS: a row whose taken cards show no progress within the bound gets one line to the coordinator naming the row, the cards and the minutes since its last progress; last progress shown in show <row> and on the dashboard; detect and tell only (new mechanism: needs the owner's agreement)")
     ("taken-over-notice-survives-restart" "TAKEN OVER survives a failed send and a restart: a durable pending-notice marker for the coordinator a take-over unhooked (LAYER-6-RUN, Taking the seat: a restart before it is sent does not send it)")
     ("coordinator-verbs-fenced-on-the-seat" "Every coordinator verb checks at commit that the caller still holds the seat: judge, land, hold, drop, policy, add, clear and unhook <row> check it only on the read, so after a take-over the old coordinator's op in flight commits; stream add, stop, start and identity are fenced (UnchangedSince Hooks)")
     )
