  (:id "t-policy-diff" :type :task :title "policy diff vA vB: a line diff of two policy versions (deleted 2026-11-08; policy show each and diff them)" :state :todo :note "was modules/policy/diff.go, a linear-space LCS refused above 10,000 lines")
  (:id "t-provider-balance-reconcile" :type :task :title "cost reconcile: provider balance falls set beside the priced API records, a cost-gap judgement hourly (deleted 2026-11-08 with modules/cost; the sprint.balances table stays)" :state :todo)
  (:id "t-land-rate-and-flap-alarms" :type :task :title "Delete the land-rate and flap alarms, the flaps column and SetRowFlaps (decision 6, not done: engine code under PR #714)" :state :todo)
  (:id "t-engine-dead-code-pass" :type :task :title "Engine dead code (dropped from the 2026-11-08 pass): card/values.go mirror of store/check.go; replay.go write-applier; WaiveRed and the red column; the Edit event; Rescore and score; Released, single AskRead, SetCardAfter, ImportedReason; the deadcode list (verbs, edge, policy, card, steps, store, worker, dash, run); schema column drops" :state :todo :note "subtraction report S11 S12 S20 S22 S24 S25 S26 S29; no branch")
  (:id "t-faults-limit-hold-witness" :type :task :title "The faults limit, its hold and the Steps limits witness (wip: model the limits step)" :state :todo :note "branch fix/engine-pr1-limits-rows (pushed 2026-11-08)")
  (:id "t-up-simplification" :type :task :title "up simplified: no two-phase handoff, no provider key step, no saved choices or --run-on, no --version adoption, no setup-time backup verify (S6 S3 S10 S14 S21)" :state :todo :note "pushed branch parked/up-simplification")
  (:id "t-stop-holds-landing-in-flight" :type :task :title "A stop holds a landing or promotion already in flight: it merges nothing until start (PR #741, parked)" :state :todo :note "branch rowan/ns-fix-stop-landing. Open: (1) the code reads the stop as of the run's last fold, up to about one tick old, so a stop inside that window still merges; Run.tla guards DeliverEdge on the store's stop, so the model should guard on the observed stop with the fold lag as its own action; (2) NoEdgeWhileStopped restates the DeliverEdge guard, no trace reaches the land goroutine, and resume-after-start has no fairness or liveness property: the model is not bound to the code; (3) what a held landing does across a clear: after stop, clear, start it may resume and merge a request from the old epoch (unverified)")
  (:id "t-add-adopts-card-branch" :type :task :title "add adopts a card's existing branch as its head, so a continuing card starts from it (PR #726, parked)" :state :todo :note "branch fix/adopt-card-branch. Open: (1) the adopted head can go stale before the first deal: the worker's push lease is the branch tip at staging (leaseFrom_internal), so commits pushed after add are overwritten; (2) any sprint/<stream>/<id> left by a dropped card or a reused id is adopted silently; (3) whether adoption is opt-in (the brief asks for it) rather than automatic, and whether a PR on a branch with another name is covered")
  (:id "t-steps-model-covers-rest" :type :task :title "Steps.tla gains the rest after faults: a resting row is offered to policy but not dealt to (the model gap under #740)" :state :todo :note "ServingOpen and Eligible have no rest term; the steps trace walk never reaches a rest (RouteRestAfter 100 in trace_test.go), so the deal's rest filter, the held unserved judgement and the no-miss answer are covered by unit tests only")
  (:id "t-next-json-answers-small" :type :task :title "next --json answers small: the finished cards of the epoch listed in brief, or only the last few (82-214 KB on nine benches on 2026-11-09, past the worker's old 64 KiB cap; the worker now reads 16 MiB and names a truncated answer, so the fix here is the size, not the parse)" :state :todo :note "modules/verbs/next.go fillInventory: Final is every done or failed consumer the row holds; the worker reads Final too (recover.go holders_internal: a finished card on disk is gone, a failed one is cancelled), so a shorter list must still name every finished card with a job on the bench")
  (:id "t-ci-flakes" :type :task :title "Functional flakes fixed: TestFunctionalClearWhileWorkersBeat (clear's seq fence refused: store at seq N+1, expected N, a beat landing between read and clear), TestFunctionalEvaluatorMemoryCap (failed once on main), a postgres start failure in a functional run; and the trace job near the 2-minute runner limit (55-130 s, cancelled on 7 of the 2026-11-09 landing runs)" :state :todo :note "each re-run only on evidence: same test, same symptom, green on main; a flake is fixed (a fence that tolerates row-only writes, a cap measured under load, a postgres start retried or its cause named), never muted")
  (:id "t-coordinator-seat-model" :type :task :title "A model of the coordinator's seat: one coordinator; hook, unhook and up --take-over, the take-over moving the seat whether the old coordinator is on the bus or gone, with a reversed witness (two coordinators at once); no module covers it (Setup.tla has the walk's steps, Store.tla the PutRow write)" :state :todo :note "added 2026-11-10 with up --take-over (asked: Add takeover to up); the take-over is unit-tested in modules/verbs/takeover_test.go; the model would own rows' sess and role and OneCoordinator")
  (:id "t-auto-down-after-missed-takes" :type :task :title "A row that misses N takes in a row is unhooked by the sprint (its hand returned) with a DOWN line to the coordinator; a take or a re-hook resets the count (new mechanism: needs the owner's agreement)" :state :todo :note "asked 2026-11-10 after aurora sat for hours re-dealt with 'in aurora's hand 180 s, not taken; back to the queue'. Proposed: N = the faults limit (3, 'consecutive faults, reset by a success'), so about 9 minutes at ready_take 180 s; a fold count of a row's consumers withdrawn with ', not taken; ', reset by a cursor take, a done report or a re-hook; the close is the existing unhook plus the hand return of PR #769; the coordinator's own row is never unhooked by it. Model first in Steps.tla: a miss count, Take/Untaken env moves, the close at the limit, an invariant that no row is dealt to past N misses, a reversed witness without the close; bound by the trace walk, which today never takes (ready_take a day), so the walk needs takes for the binding to mean anything")
  (:id "t-no-progress-line" :type :task :title "NO-PROGRESS: a row whose taken cards show no progress within the bound gets one line to the coordinator naming the row, the cards and the minutes since its last progress; last progress shown in show <row> and on the dashboard; detect and tell only (new mechanism: needs the owner's agreement)" :state :todo :note "asked 2026-11-10 (holding cards and answering bus challenges is not work); never a release or an unhook for lack of progress. Proposed bound: the card's tier deadline, ready_take + the consumer time of its tier (flash 900 s, pro 2700, heavy 5400, frontier 7200). The store keeps no push or head history, so progress is a report or a finish unless head moves are recorded; say so in the line. A per-row last progress folded from events, published to the dashboard feed beside landings; model with a reversed witness (a silent row never told)")
  (:id "t-taken-over-notice-survives-restart" :type :task :title "TAKEN OVER survives a failed send and a restart: a durable pending-notice marker for the coordinator a take-over unhooked (LAYER-6-RUN, Taking the seat: a restart before it is sent does not send it)" :state :todo :note "found 2026-11-10 on PR #778: CatchUp's replay floor (modules/run/push.go) is the lowest cursor of the rows hooked in, so once they are pushed past the take-over its event is never replayed for the unhooked row. Weighed: the floor at every push cursor (5 lines, but a long-gone row's cursor drags every restart back without bound, and a coordinator with no cursor is still missed); a marker the take-over op writes (new durable state shared by verbs and run); holding other cursors below an unsent take-over notice (a cursor protocol change, outside Run.tla's fixed recipients)")
  (:id "t-coordinator-verbs-fenced-on-the-seat" :type :task :title "Every coordinator verb checks at commit that the caller still holds the seat: judge, land, hold, drop, policy, add, clear and unhook <row> check it only on the read, so after a take-over the old coordinator's op in flight commits; stream add, stop, start and identity are fenced (UnchangedSince Hooks)" :state :todo :note "found 2026-11-10 on PR #778 (a take-over needs nothing from the old coordinator, so it can be mid-verb); the record fences on the cards and judgements still hold, only the authority is stale; also unhold, priority, relink, replace and stream set (moves.go commits steps.Verb's op, which checks the coordinator on the snapshot, steps/request.go); TestCoordinatorVerbsFencedOnTheirHook states the intent for the fenced three")))
